course: dictionary
lesson: 4733
title: Hornet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hornet is a large wasp, often yellow and brown or black, with a powerful sting. The word wasp tells you the basic kind of insect, and large tells you it is bigger than a common wasp.
explain: Read the context to check. «The European hornet is the biggest wasp in Ukraine and is usually calmer than small wasps; it stings only if its nest is disturbed.» The clues show that hornets are big, that they are often calm, and that they sting mainly to defend their nest.
explain: Some phrases mean more than their words. «Stir up a hornet's nest» does not mean you touch a real nest. It means you cause a lot of trouble and anger. Test it by putting your meaning into the sentence and checking that it still makes sense.
fact: A hornet is a large wasp with a powerful sting.
fact: Hornets build big paper nests, and only the young queens survive the winter.
fact: The Asian giant hornet attacks honeybee hives, so scientists tracked it and destroyed its nests.
fact: «Stir up a hornet's nest» means to cause a lot of trouble and anger.
fact: If you see a hornet, keep away from its nest, stay calm and walk away slowly.
exercise: What is a hornet? | *A large wasp with a powerful sting | A kind of bee that makes honey | A type of spider with eight legs | A small bird that builds nests in trees
exercise: According to the text, when does a hornet sting? | *Only if its nest is disturbed, squashed or grabbed | Only when it is hungry for honey | Only at night, when it is dark | Every time it sees a person
exercise: The phrase «stir up a hornet's nest» means: | To count how many hornets live in one nest | *To cause a lot of trouble and anger | To sit very still and wait quietly | To build a new nest in spring
test: What are hornet nests made of? | Wax from honeybees | Mud and grass | *Paper | Leaves and twigs
test: «Each queen starts a new nest alone, and an old nest is not used again.» Why does a queen build a new nest in spring? | Queens sleep in the same nest all year | Her old nest is always used again | *Old nests are not used again, so she starts a new one | She wants to be near the honeybees
exam: What should you do if you meet a hornet near its nest? | Poke the nest to see inside | Run quickly and wave your arms | *Keep away, stay calm and walk away slowly | Throw stones at it
